cff-version: 1.2.0
title: earnings_surprise_analyzer
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Lyonn
    family-names: Lie
    alias: leeyawnnn
repository-code: https://github.com/leeyawnnn/earnings_surprise_analyzer
abstract: >-
  An event study of post-earnings announcement drift on US equities. Earnings
  releases are dated by the acceptance timestamp of the 8-K carrying item 2.02,
  and surprise is measured as standardised unexpected earnings built from
  first-reported XBRL figures, so both are point-in-time. Inference is
  corrected for overlapping event windows and for correlation within an
  earnings season, and the backtest is marked daily and costed.
keywords:
  - event study
  - post-earnings announcement drift
  - quantitative finance
  - backtesting
  - equity research
